{"step_index":663,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-20T17:55:45Z","thinking":"**Analyzing the Visual Layout**\n\nOkay, so I've been digging into the codebase. I was initially looking for a secondary bar, but the layout in `(portal)/layout.tsx` is, in fact, the unified top header. Looking again at the user's screenshot, I can see the \"Hiện trạng\" and \"Lộ trình\" items, which are consistent with the code in `src/app/(portal`.\n\n\n**Reimagining the Navigation**\n\nOkay, I'm now exploring alternative placements for the navigation. My current thought is to replace the top header with the logo on the left and the \"Quản trị\" button on the right, and the `Segmented` control centered within the main content. This would replace the existing `navItems.map` within the current top header.\n\n\n**Refining the UI Placement**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the `Segmented` control's integration. Currently, it's rendered within `(portal)/layout.tsx`. I believe I can reposition it to maintain its functionality, but streamline the visual flow. I'm exploring how to best integrate it into the UI with the top header, or whether it might need to reside elsewhere, with `Segmented`'s state maintained by the router. I am focused on minimizing redundant code.\n\n\n**Evaluating the Component Structure**\n\nI am now focusing on the header and `Segmented` component's layout. Specifically, I'm examining how to optimally incorporate the logo, \"Khung Kiến trúc Số\" text, and \"Quản trị\" button, along with the segmented control into a cohesive user experience. My current inclination is to restructure the header to centralize these controls, using the existing code block in `/src/app/(portal)/layout.tsx` as my point of reference. I am now evaluating the positioning of each element.\n\n\n**Confirming the Page Header**\n\nI've been reviewing the placement and impact of the `Segmented` control, specifically within the `PortalLayout`. My key insight is that putting the `Segmented` control directly within the `<main>` element, above the `children`, is actually the optimal position. I need to make sure the headers of the individual pages like `hien-trang` and `lo-trinh` look great beneath the control. So I checked `hien-trang/page.tsx`'s header to ensure compatibility.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"use client\";\nimport Link from \"next/link\";\nimport { usePathname, useRouter } from \"next/navigation\";\nimport { ApartmentOutlined } from \"@ant-design/icons\";\nimport { Button, Segmented } from \"antd\";\n\nexport default function PortalLayout({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {\n  const pathname = usePathname();\n  const router = useRouter();\n\n  // Xác định view hiện tại để set giá trị cho Segmented\n  const currentValue = pathname.includes(\"/kts/lo-trinh\") ? \"lo-trinh\" : \"hien-trang\";\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"min-h-screen bg-gray-50\">\n      <header className=\"bg-white border-b shadow-sm sticky top-0 z-50\">\n        <div className=\"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 py-3 flex items-center justify-between\">\n          <Link href=\"/\" className=\"flex items-center gap-2 hover:opacity-80 transition-opacity\">\n            <div className=\"w-8 h-8 bg-blue-800 rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center shadow-inner\">\n              <ApartmentOutlined className=\"text-white text-sm\" />\n            </div>\n            <div className=\"leading-tight\">\n              <div className=\"font-bold text-blue-900 text-sm\">KTS Vĩnh Long</div>\n              <div className=\"text-gray-400 text-xs\">Khung Kiến trúc Số</div>\n            </div>\n          </Link>\n          \n          <div className=\"flex gap-2\">\n            <Link href=\"/admin\">\n              <Button type=\"primary\" size=\"small\" style={{ backgroundColor: \"#003087\" }}>\n                Quản trị\n              </Button>\n            </Link>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </header>